  "truthSource": "manual_audit",
  "truthReference": "RE-AUDITED for M14 #288. Every fact below was re-derived by hand from validation/m12/fixtures/html/*.html against HTML5 semantics and the M14 #288 identity contract, and each carries a `reference` quoting the source text it was read from. This is NOT a transcription of analyzer output: each row was decided from the markup first, then compared against the live analyzer, and the two places where they disagreed were investigated rather than resolved in the analyzer's favour. The audit changed five rulings the previous truth asserted: (1) the document IS the module, so there is a module symbol and the document root is a containment source; (2) a duplicate `id` is still an addressable element and is named `<id>#N` instead of being dropped; (3) a form endpoint is `uses`, never `calls`; (4) a `javascript:` URL is a genuine hazard and DOES emit a row; (5) an EXTERNAL absolute URL (https:, mailto:, tel:) is not a dependency of this codebase and emits nothing. The `href=\"#\"` case is absent from BOTH the analyzer and the oracle and is pinned in html/scheme-and-navigation instead: `#` names the top of this document, which the document module already is. Audit scope: both fixtures in full, every symbol and every relationship. Regenerating this file from analyzer output would destroy its value as an independent check.",
